# Golden / fixture files are byte-exact artifacts, compared verbatim by tests.
# Force LF and never CRLF-translate them: they are generated with LF-terminated
# lines, and a Windows checkout would otherwise translate the committed goldens
# to CRLF, so a freshly-rendered (LF) result would spuriously mismatch. The SVG
# parity gate caught exactly this on its first Windows run — this is the fix.
Tests/fixtures/svg-golden/*.svg text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures (the VDL1 wire corpus) must never be touched at all.
*.bin binary
